      "label": "(b)",
      "marks": 2,
      "answer": "They are not independent.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "$P(A)P(B)=\\frac13\\times\\frac{10}{36}=\\frac{5}{54}$ (M1; both probabilities and product seen). Since $\\frac{5}{54}\\ne\\frac{5}{36}=P(A\\cap B)$, the events are not independent (A1; both values, $P(A)P(B)$ and $P(A\\cap B)$ seen with correct conclusion; condone $\\frac{5}{36}$ stated in (a)). Alternative: $P(B\\mid A)=\\frac{5/36}{1/3}=\\frac{5}{12}\\ne\\frac{10}{36}=P(B)$, so not independent (M1 A1; equivalent conditional method and correct conclusion; condone equivalent fraction identified in (a)). [2]",
      "structured": {
        "version": 1,
        "sections": [
          {
            "label": "Main method",
            "steps": [
